    @* HeadOutlet carries each page's <PageTitle>, so it must come first: a browser
       uses the FIRST <title> in the document.

       The literal title below it is only a fallback, and its position matters for
       the same reason. Pages that disable prerendering (prerender:false, such as
       Index and LecturerHome) render no title at all on the server, because
       nothing is server rendered for HeadOutlet to pick up. Without this
       fallback they were left with an empty tab title, showing the raw URL to a
       lecturer juggling several tabs.

       When such a page's circuit starts, Blazor replaces document.title with the
       page's own, so the fallback is only ever visible for an instant. *@
    <HeadOutlet />
    <title>VIIDII</title>
</head>
<body>
    <Routes />
    <div id="blazor-error-ui">
        An unhandled error has occurred.
        <a href="" class="reload">Reload</a>
        <a class="dismiss">🗙</a>
    </div>

    <script src="lib/bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
    <script src="lib/signalr/signalr.min.js"></script>
    <script src="js/sessionInterop.js?v=20261015e"></script>
@* PeerJS is no longer loaded. The peer-to-peer mesh it provided required the free
   public 0.peerjs.com cloud for signalling, had no relay fallback, and the code had
   no way to point it anywhere else. It failed on every real phone. LiveKit replaces
   it and brings its own signalling and relays. *@
    <script src="js/livekitInterop.js?v=20261015e"></script>
    <script src="js/captionInterop.js?v=20261015e"></script>
    <script src="js/viidii-ui.js?v=20261013d"></script>


</body>
</html>
